      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 6 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -9 & -2 & -9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -9 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_{3}:=-8R_{3}$ on $X?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation $R_{3}:=-8R_{3}$ means that we need to multiply the third row of the matrix by $-8.$\n\nMultiplying the $3$rd row by $-8$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X &= \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 6 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -9 & -2 & -9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -9 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{3}:=-8R_{3} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 6 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -9 & -2 & -9 & -8 \\\\ -8\\cdot 0 & -8\\cdot (-9) & -8\\cdot (-9) & -8\\cdot (-3)\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 6 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -9 & -2 & -9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 72 & 72 & 24\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
